    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0793" n="1627" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">War Trade Board Files: Shipping and Tonnage,
                    Switzerland, Vol. I</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the War Trade Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >McCormick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Swiss
                        Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sulzer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I am in receipt of your
                    letter of May 31, dealing further with the points raised by our earlier
                    correspondence on the subject of the steamers <hi rendition="#italic">Hans
                        Mœrsk</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Oluf Mœrsk</hi>. In deference to your
                    very urgent representations arrangements have now been made whereby these two
                    steamers may be chartered to your Government for a round trip to Cette for the
                    transport of a general cargo including gasoline and kerosene. In view of the
                    fact that we have thus been able to meet your Government’s wishes in this
                    matter, I do not feel that it is necessary to go into the other points.</p>
                <p>I wish to express my appreciation of your very kind expressions relative to the
                    efforts being made by my Government to insure the <pb facs="0794" n="1628"
                        xml:id="pg1628"/> receipt by Switzerland of necessary supplies, and the
                    withdrawal of our objections to the charter by your Government of the two
                    steamers above mentioned, is in accord with our general policy of demonstrating
                    in as practicable manner as possible the sincerity of our friendship for the
                    Swiss Government.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vance McCormick</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
